{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530218-developer-diary-8-some-interesting-news-about-bloodlines-2","id":1530218,"title":"Developer Diary 8#: Some interesting news about Bloodlines 2","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-07T16:17:35-08:00","id":1530218,"title":"Developer Diary 8#: Some interesting news about Bloodlines 2","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/news/explore-the-world-of-darkness\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://images.ctfassets.net/u73tyf0fa8v1/4GtNkTwc3KD5wcl5iZfw6H/412090a992d51ec9d468cacc1ccfab7a/bloodlines2-web-header.webp?w=1200&amp;h=630&amp;fit=fill&amp;f=center\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/news/explore-the-world-of-darkness\" target=\"_blank\"> Dev Diary #8: Explore the World of Darkness - Paradox Interactive </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/news/explore-the-world-of-darkness\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/news/explore-the-world-of-darkness </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines 2 - You are the Nomad. An elder vampire awakening from a century-long slumber, new to the modern nights. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> They've decided to explain more about the plot and roleplaying.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Re: Seattle</b></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Our goal with this pillar was to create a version of Seattle that is authentic to The World of Darkness IP and makes you believe that this hidden side of Seattle, where vampires are in control, could be real and that in contrast the human world feels more alien to you and potentially unreal. To that end, we didn't set about making an exact replica of Seattle, as our priority wasn't to represent the human world, but the vampire one. The Seattle you experience in Bloodlines 2 is a kind of &quot;best-of&quot; Seattle where we've taken key landmarks and brought them in closer together. For example, Pioneer Square is a key location, and it speaks to us of the old city and its founders (some of which were vampires that you will meet), but we also have volunteer park, which in reality is on the outskirts of the city but we loved the idea of doing a creepy mission there that reveals something sinister beneath this iconic conservatory.] </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Re: Clan Politics</b></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Bloodlines 1 you were a new vampire in a city with a large Anarch presence where the Camarilla don\u2019t have complete dominance. For Bloodlines 2 we have flipped this on its head. You play Phyre, an Elder vampire (~400 years old) in a city where Camarilla has been dominant for decades, and any hint of Anarch sympathy is squashed. Phyre's number 1 loyalty is to herself, but she is wise enough to respect the power of the Camarilla and, more importantly, the Masquerade. Within the story Phyre earns a seat at the top-table of the Camarilla as the court's Sheriff, giving her the court's protection but also a powerful authority within Seattle's vampire society. This is an RPG, of course, so you can roleplay Sheriff in multiple ways, maybe you are a loyal Sheriff of the Camarilla, or an Anarch sympathiser working from within to undermine the court, or maybe you're a self-centred Elder vampire playing the different factions off each other to your advantage. </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Re:: Phyre's Character</span></b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Phyre's motivation in the story is driven (at least initially) by regaining her power - she has awoken after 100 years in torpor (vampire hibernation) 6000 miles from home with markings all over her body which are limiting her powers. This sets up the narrative context of the ability tree (which we will show in due course) which instead of being about adding new powers to Phyre, like levelling up in the pen-and-paper RPG, you are unlocking her existing powers. Over her 300 years roaming the old world, Phyre had gained many powers, not only those from the disciplines of her clan.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T05:10:56-08:00","id":1530369,"title":"","content":"I must say that making the protagonist of this game an elder, rather than a fledgling struck me from the first as a very sensible one - after all, it\u2019s more credible that a newly awakened elder can make a dramatic impression on their surroundings than that a fledging could wreck havoc singlehanded - though one would have appreciated a more customisable avatar.<br /> <br /> For some reason playing female characters in video games always leaves me feeling embarrassed and a little guilty: perhaps because playing someone of my own gender feels more like slipping on a costume and doing a little amateur dramatics, while playing as a lady feels more like mind controlling some poor soul.<br /> <br /> Human psychology is a tangled thicket full of oddities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T02:25:18-08:00","id":1530425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530218-developer-diary-8-some-interesting-news-about-bloodlines-2?p=1530369#post1530369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must say that making the protagonist of this game an elder, rather than a fledgling struck me from the first as a very sensible one - after all, it\u2019s more credible that a newly awakened elder can make a dramatic impression on their surroundings than that a fledging could wreck havoc singlehanded - though one would have appreciated a more customisable avatar.<br /> <br /> For some reason playing female characters in video games always leaves me feeling embarrassed and a little guilty: perhaps because playing someone of my own gender feels more like slipping on a costume and doing a little amateur dramatics, while playing as a lady feels more like mind controlling some poor soul.<br /> <br /> Human psychology is a tangled thicket full of oddities.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should know that the game presumably gives you the option to either play as male or female. And from the looks of the concept-art you can change things like the hair. Of course, we've only seen that in concept-art thus far. We haven't seen the male voice/model in action or been shown the character-creation-screen. And the descriptions always refer to Phyre as she. I don't think that's a good preview-strategy but alas, it's the one they chose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T03:07:15-08:00","id":1530429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530218-developer-diary-8-some-interesting-news-about-bloodlines-2?p=1530425#post1530425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You should know that the game presumably gives you the option to either play as male or female. And from the looks of the concept-art you can change things like the hair. Of course, we've only seen that in concept-art thus far. We haven't seen the male voice/model in action or been shown the character-creation-screen. And the descriptions always refer to Phyre as she. I don't think that's a good preview-strategy but alas, it's the one they chose.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may have too much faith in the Chinese Room but I suspect that this will be a case where the game is going to be released with limited options and they will gradually add more like more customization, the other Clans and so on.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T03:24:56-08:00","id":1530430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530218-developer-diary-8-some-interesting-news-about-bloodlines-2?p=1530429#post1530429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I may have too much faith in the Chinese Room but I suspect that this will be a case where the game is going to be released with limited options and they will gradually add more like more customization, the other Clans and so on.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe... but that rarely ends well for these kinds of games. It's also a question of money: To what degree is Paradox willing to pay them to keep working on the game beyond the release of the game? I would also feel bad for the developers because in these scenarios the game would be released with bad reviews and then the publisher is just like &quot;Okay, guys, the reviews are bad, the game didn't sell as much as we'd like... let's pull the plug!&quot;. Redfall, Marvel's Avengers, Anthem, Saints Row (2023)... The publisher insisted on the game being pushed out the door despite the flaws because the hope/assumption is that it can all be fixed post-release. And then the games just land with a thud upon release-day and people just lose interest and the sales-numbers never recover. And then the publisher is just fine with cutting their losses and move on. It's very rare for a game to turn things around after a bad launch. Only two come to my mind where that worked recently: Cyberpunk 2077 and No Man's Sky. The former has a rich studio behind it and got boosted by things like the surprise-success of an anime and the latter just crawled its way back to goodness because a dedicated team of developers kept working on it post-release for years.<br /> <br /> But the norm is: If you release your game in an unfinished state (that equals to: a huge amount of bugs, missing features, descriptions of the game not matching with the released game) - it just fails. So, let's hope Bloodlines 2 won't be like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T04:04:36-08:00","id":1530432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530218-developer-diary-8-some-interesting-news-about-bloodlines-2?p=1530430#post1530430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe... but that rarely ends well for these kinds of games. It's also a question of money: To what degree is Paradox willing to pay them to keep working on the game beyond the release of the game? I would also feel bad for the developers because in these scenarios the game would be released with bad reviews and then the publisher is just like &quot;Okay, guys, the reviews are bad, the game didn't sell as much as we'd like... let's pull the plug!&quot;. Redfall, Marvel's Avengers, Anthem, Saints Row (2023)... The publisher insisted on the game being pushed out the door despite the flaws because the hope/assumption is that it can all be fixed post-release. And then the games just land with a thud upon release-day and people just lose interest and the sales-numbers never recover. And then the publisher is just fine with cutting their losses and move on. It's very rare for a game to turn things around after a bad launch. Only two come to my mind where that worked recently: Cyberpunk 2077 and No Man's Sky. The former has a rich studio behind it and got boosted by things like the surprise-success of an anime and the latter just crawled its way back to goodness because a dedicated team of developers kept working on it post-release for years.<br /> <br /> But the norm is: If you release your game in an unfinished state (that equals to: a huge amount of bugs, missing features, descriptions of the game not matching with the released game) - it just fails. So, let's hope Bloodlines 2 won't be like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a limit to Paradox's patience but I think they get tarred with a lot of other game developer's shit. Paradox notably DIDNT release Bloodlines 2 as a buggy half-completed mess but pulled the plug on it.<br /> <br /> They fired Hardsuit Labs for doing a shitty job.<br /> <br /> And they seem to have given as much time as The Chinese Room has needed to get the game finished in a proper state.<br /> <br /> Which is VERY unusual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T04:27:23-08:00","id":1530433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530218-developer-diary-8-some-interesting-news-about-bloodlines-2?p=1530432#post1530432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a limit to Paradox's patience but I think they get tarred with a lot of other game developer's shit. Paradox notably DIDNT release Bloodlines 2 as a buggy half-completed mess but pulled the plug on it.<br /> <br /> They fired Hardsuit Labs for doing a shitty job.<br /> <br /> And they seem to have given as much time as The Chinese Room has needed to get the game finished in a proper state.<br /> <br /> Which is VERY unusual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they get tarred with these negative implications because the stuff I talked about in my previous post aren't problems linked to particular publishers/developers, they're <i>videogame-industry-problems</i>.<br /> <br /> And case in point: Paradox. Lamplighter's League, Cities: Skyline 2, recent DLC for Europa Universalis IV - all of them Paradox releases that launched with big problems when it comes to bugs, features and performance. So yes, Paradox is absolutely a candidate who would sign off on a shitty launch. If anything, recent releases with Paradox as a publisher are making it more likely that Bloodlines 2 will have a bad launch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T05:27:06-08:00","id":1530437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530218-developer-diary-8-some-interesting-news-about-bloodlines-2?p=1530369#post1530369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must say that making the protagonist of this game an elder, rather than a fledgling struck me from the first as a very sensible one - after all, it\u2019s more credible that a newly awakened elder can make a dramatic impression on their surroundings than that a fledging could wreck havoc singlehanded - though one would have appreciated a more customisable avatar.<br /> <br /> For some reason playing female characters in video games always leaves me feeling embarrassed and a little guilty: perhaps because playing someone of my own gender feels more like slipping on a costume and doing a little amateur dramatics, while playing as a lady feels more like mind controlling some poor soul.<br /> <br /> Human psychology is a tangled thicket full of oddities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since you (presumably) identify as male irl, you probably feel somewhat disconnected when playing a female character. Just a hunch though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 02-10-2024, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T08:03:03-08:00","id":1530444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530218-developer-diary-8-some-interesting-news-about-bloodlines-2?p=1530437#post1530437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since you (presumably) identify as male irl, you probably feel somewhat disconnected when playing a female character. Just a hunch though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if 1st or 3rd person perspective plays a role. Lots of men love playing Lara Croft after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T08:37:20-08:00","id":1530450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530218-developer-diary-8-some-interesting-news-about-bloodlines-2?p=1530444#post1530444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder if 1st or 3rd person perspective plays a role. Lots of men love playing Lara Croft after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That takes me back to crude summations comparing Ultima's over the shoulder outing to Tomb Raider. Apparently, the spear side didn't find the Avatar's hinder as appealing as Lara's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T17:32:15-08:00","id":1530505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530218-developer-diary-8-some-interesting-news-about-bloodlines-2?p=1530433#post1530433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cities: Skyline 2</div> </div> </div> </div>Even with Paradox's reputation for pushing out games in an unfinished, buggy state, I'm still kind of shocked and disappointed with that one. I was really looking forward to it but it was just a mess. I'm glad I was able to refund it after playing it for a couple of hours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T12:58:45-08:00","id":1530579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530218-developer-diary-8-some-interesting-news-about-bloodlines-2?p=1530505#post1530505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even with Paradox's reputation for pushing out games in an unfinished, buggy state, I'm still kind of shocked and disappointed with that one. I was really looking forward to it but it was just a mess. I'm glad I was able to refund it after playing it for a couple of hours.</div> </div> </div> </div>That wasn't a Paradox game I was interested in but the reviews and gameplay I saw didn't look great...<br /> <br /> And that's another problem with the whole &quot;We'll fix this post-launch&quot;-approach. When you have this disastrous launch, all these plans for DLC... you can just throw 'em in the trash. Rather than working on expanding the game and adding new features, the development team will be busy fixing the base-game first. That's the situation Cities Skyline 2 finds itself in. And Bloodlines 2 will suffer a similar fate if it launches in a bad/unfinished state (the release-date of those two planned DLC will get pushed back, of course).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T02:58:44-08:00","id":1530621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530218-developer-diary-8-some-interesting-news-about-bloodlines-2?p=1530437#post1530437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since you (presumably) identify as male irl, you probably feel somewhat disconnected when playing a female character. Just a hunch though.</div> </div> </div> </div> Very true, as inferred by my original post: I suppose it doesn\u2019t help that most video game characters are built to be very good-looking, which ups the \u2018What are your intentions toward that young lady?\u2019 factor even more potent.<br /> <br /> Clearly I\u2019m just an old-fashioned gentleman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T03:01:05-08:00","id":1530622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530218-developer-diary-8-some-interesting-news-about-bloodlines-2?p=1530444#post1530444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder if 1st or 3rd person perspective plays a role. Lots of men love playing Lara Croft after all.</div> </div> </div> </div> I did play one or two TOMB RAIDER games back in the day: that was <i>before</i> I went through puberty and also decided that Mind Control was one of my very least favourite fictional tropes (The only thing I hate more is Time Travel).<br /> <br /> Hopefully that\u2019s a harmless eccentricity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T01:18:45-07:00","id":1536952,"title":"","content":"I'm a pessimistic, and cynical individual, as you will be able to ascertain from my posting history, but I wish the Chinese Room good luck. This is a beloved property, that has been delayed for a very, very long time.<br /> <br /> But, naming the protagonist, that you have very little control of's indentity... Phyre? With the 90's edgelord &quot;Phy?&quot; Why not name &quot;Them&quot; Blimp Fizkit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}